Context
  Licence chosen by surveying the sibling repositories rather than by picking
  a default, at the owner's instruction ("look through our other public repos
  and pick one to align: i think MIT is fine").

Census of the 28 public dsp-dr repositories, via the REST licence endpoint
  9  MIT            (including this one, after this commit)
  3  NOASSERTION    licence text that GitHub cannot match exactly
  2  GPL-3.0
  1  Apache-2.0     hegel-guile
  13 none
  MIT is therefore the house default among those that carry one.

Alignment target
  dsp-dr/guile-skills, the most recently licensed sibling. LICENSE here is a
  byte-for-byte copy, SHA-256
  4bfcd490354f46118d11fedd49a951bfc8328d6a7fa176a93321d37d20cf3e82, so the
  copyright line reads "Copyright (c) 2026 dsp-dr". Older siblings use
  inconsistent holder styles (DSP-DR, DevOps Team, "guile-sage contributors");
  the lowercase account name is the current one. The text is
  normalisation-identical to GitHub's canonical MIT body, ASCII, LF endings.
  The README's License section copies guile-sage's wording.

  Note that the holder is the account, not the commit author: commits here are
  authored by Daria Pascal <dpascal@defrecord.com>, but the house convention
  puts the GitHub account in the copyright line.

Two measurement errors made while establishing the above, recorded so the
numbers are not trusted blindly next time
  1. The first survey used GraphQL (gh repo list --json licenseInfo) and
     reported all 28 repositories as unlicensed, which led to the wrong
     conclusion that there was nothing to align with. That field returns an
     object with a null spdxId here and paginates inconsistently. It is not
     reliable; the REST endpoint repos/OWNER/REPO/licence is.
  2. A follow-up per-repository check used .license.spdxId on the REST
     endpoint, where the field is snake_case .license.spdx_id, and so printed
     empty for every repository that does in fact carry a licence.
  GitHub's detection is also asynchronous: this repository reported no licence
  immediately after the push and MIT shortly afterwards. An immediate "not
  detected" means nothing.
